From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] soc: qcom: pmic-glink: trace raw altmode messages

Log the PMIC-GLINK message header before the altmode parser handles it. This
distinguishes a missing firmware notification from a notification rejected by
the Linux parser. The change is diagnostic only.

---
 drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
index 4bc867dbd801..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -522,6 +522,11 @@ static void pmic_glink_altmode_callback(const void *data, size_t len, void *priv)
 	opcode = le32_to_cpu(hdr->opcode) & 0xff;
 	svid = le32_to_cpu(hdr->opcode) >> 16;
+
+	dev_info(altmode->dev,
+		 "raw altmode message owner=%u type=%u opcode=0x%02x svid=0x%04x len=%zu\n",
+		 le32_to_cpu(hdr->owner), le32_to_cpu(hdr->type), opcode, svid,
+		 len);
 
 	switch (opcode) {
-- 
